	(text "VBUS_SENSE divider (10k / 15k)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 196.85 33.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1ab8c2d4-7979-5442-8af4-a6acf7a04165")
	)
	(text "D+/D- series pair - no ESD array"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 116.84 60.96 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "334939c5-bb9b-5e8e-a24e-3fda902f9b02")
	)
	(text "D21 / R56 - USB POWER INDICATOR, THE ONLY LED ON THIS BOARD BESIDES THE WS2812C. USB_VBUS -> R56 1 k ->\nUSB_LED_A -> D21 anode, cathode to GND, so it lights whenever a host is plugged in and is dark on BEC-only\npower - which is exactly the question a bench user asks of this connector, and one the RGB status LED cannot\nanswer because D20 runs off V5_SYS and lights on either source.\nD21 IS A WHITE 0603 (KT-0603W, LCSC C2290, JLC BASIC), NOT BLUE: JLC stocks no Basic blue LED, and a colour\nis not worth a per-unique-part Extended setup fee on an indicator (DESIGN_SPEC \"Decisions\").\nOPERATING POINT: VF 2.6-3.1 V at 5 mA (datasheet 360 mcd at 5 mA), so at VBUS 5.0 V through R56 1 k the current\nis (5.0 - 2.9) / 1k ~ 2 mA and the part is run at about 40 %% of its test current - dim by indicator standards,\ndeliberately: R56 is the 1 k line the board already buys (LCSC C11702, shared with R21/R24/R53/R54) and 2 mA\noff USB is 10 mW that costs the host nothing. It is NOT a rail health indicator: it says \"VBUS is present\",\nnot \"the regulators are up\"."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 10 173.794 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "50413a28-61dc-5c04-a6c7-79cdf09c19b1")
	)
	(text "USB_VBUS feeds the D1 Schottky and the Q1 gate on POWER 2 directly; no inrush or current limiting on this\nsheet, and no data ESD array any more - U8 USBLC6-2SC6 was JLC Extended and is removed (DESIGN_SPEC \"Decisions\"),\nso D+/D- go straight from J4 into the 27 R series pair R22/R23, as on the madflight FC3v2. The RP2354B USB pins\ncarry their own on-die ESD structures; a board-level array is what this design gives up, deliberately."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 10 164.461 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5c2f5459-b12a-57a7-a883-23aa6bfd4c50")
	)
	(text "SWD landing pads"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 196.85 113.03 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6fce170a-7ff0-5d89-81c1-cdf5813497b9")
	)
	(text "CC pull-downs"
